# refund-ui environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in values for local development.
# Never commit .env.local or any file with real secrets.

# URL of the refund-api backend service (T14, specs/007-refund-service).
# Local default: the refund-api service started via `bun run dev` in the
# refund-api/ directory (plan.md: base http://localhost:8082 local).
# Production: set to the deployed refund-api URL (EU region — data residency,
# CLAUDE.md), e.g. https://api.refund.operai.io.
#
# Read directly via `import.meta.env.VITE_REFUND_API_URL` in
# src/lib/refundApi.ts (own env, own build — mirrors estimai-ui's
# VITE_API_URL, NOT admin-ui's shell-sourced getAuthBaseUrl(): refund-api is a
# sibling resource server like estimai-api, not the auth service, so there is
# no federated getter for it). Authenticated calls still go through the
# shared `shell/session` `apiFetch` (Bearer attach + 401 refresh-retry,
# ADR-0001/ADR-0006) — see that file's doc comment for a DRIFT note: the
# shell's own trusted-origins allowlist (shell/src/lib/session.ts) does not
# yet include a refund-api origin, so apiFetch will not attach the Bearer JWT
# to these requests until that allowlist is updated (out of this task's
# `refund-ui/src/` scope).
VITE_REFUND_API_URL=http://localhost:8082

# Runtime remoteEntry.js URL for the shell host (mirrors estimai-ui/admin-ui's
# SHELL_REMOTE_URL pattern — see vite.config.ts). Read via `process.env`, NOT
# `import.meta.env` (it configures Vite itself, Node-side). Dev-only default
# is baked into vite.config.ts.
# SHELL_REMOTE_URL=http://localhost:5173/remoteEntry.js
